1
00:01:58,970 --> 00:02:01,090
My name

2
00:02:01,730 --> 00:02:03,980
is Grey Worm.

3
00:02:05,690 --> 00:02:07,390
I come from

4
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,860
the Summer "Ills."

5
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:12,420
Isles.

6
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:15,700
Summer Isles.

7
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:19,070
Summer Isles.

8
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:29,270
I am from an island called Naath.

9
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:34,100
When they took you?

10
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:37,200
"When did they take me?"

11
00:02:40,010 --> 00:02:42,190
I was five years old.

12
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,580
You remember your home?

13
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:48,690
I remember when they rowed us away from shore.

14
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:54,330
How white the beaches were.

15
00:02:55,810 --> 00:02:57,780
How tall the trees.

16
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,680
And I remember my village burning.

17
00:03:05,130 --> 00:03:07,660
Smoke rising into the sky.

18
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,250
Do you remember your home?

19
00:03:19,350 --> 00:03:20,510
Unsullied.

20
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:23,140
Always Unsullied.

21
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,700
Before Unsullied, nothing.

22
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,540
That's not true.

23
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,780
Perhaps one day you will return to the Summer Isles.

24
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,410
I don't want return.

25
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,400
Kill the masters.

26
00:03:42,810 --> 00:03:44,580
Kill the masters.

27
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:48,160
How are the lessons coming?

28
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:51,470
Very well, Your Grace.

29
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:54,770
Missandei is teacher good, my queen.

30
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,660
You'll have to continue later.

31
00:04:02,390 --> 00:04:03,580
It's time.

32
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:56,940
Mhysa! Mhysa! Mhysa!

33
00:07:56,940 --> 00:08:00,450
Mhysa! Mhysa! Mhysa! Mhysa!

34
00:08:00,450 --> 00:08:02,710
Mhysa! Mhysa!

35
00:08:42,610 --> 00:08:44,080
Remind me, Ser Jorah,

36
00:08:44,170 --> 00:08:48,060
how many children did the Great Masters nail to mileposts?

37
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:50,270
163, Khaleesi.

38
00:08:51,410 --> 00:08:52,890
Yes, that was it.

39
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:03,800
Your Grace, may I have a word?

40
00:09:09,870 --> 00:09:11,270
The city is yours.

41
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,950
All these people, they're your subjects now.

42
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:17,810
Sometimes it is better to answer injustice

43
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:19,900
with mercy.

44
00:09:20,170 --> 00:09:23,930
I will answer injustice with justice.

45
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:43,970
What the hell was that?

46
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:47,470
That was me knocking your ass to the dirt

47
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:49,300
with your own hand.

48
00:10:52,470 --> 00:10:53,960
You're a rare talent.

49
00:10:54,390 --> 00:10:56,220
When you're fighting cripples, anyway.

50
00:10:58,210 --> 00:11:00,240
You learned to fight like a good little boy.

51
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:01,410
I'll bet that thrust through

52
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:03,760
the Mad King's back was pretty as a picture.

53
00:11:03,790 --> 00:11:05,790
You want to fight pretty or you want to win?

54
00:11:05,870 --> 00:11:07,630
You talk to my brother this way?

55
00:11:07,690 --> 00:11:08,910
All the time.

56
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:10,960
He got used to it.

57
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:20,490
Do you think he did it?

58
00:11:21,460 --> 00:11:22,420
No.

59
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:25,930
Oh, he hated the little twat, sure.

60
00:11:26,330 --> 00:11:28,080
But who didn't?

61
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,090
And poison's not his style.

62
00:11:32,190 --> 00:11:33,890
Or murder, for that matter.

63
00:11:36,210 --> 00:11:38,080
You want to know for sure, why don't you ask him?

64
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:45,000
You haven't been to see him yet, eh?

65
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:47,310
We're done for today.

66
00:11:51,070 --> 00:11:53,820
Your brother ever tell you how I came into his service?

67
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:56,450
You stood for him in his trial by combat at the Eyrie.

68
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:58,000
Aye.

69
00:11:58,610 --> 00:12:03,200
But only when Lady Arryn demanded the trial take place that day.

70
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:05,500
You were his first choice.

71
00:12:06,410 --> 00:12:07,910
He named you for his champion,

72
00:12:07,910 --> 00:12:11,390
because he knew you would ride day and night to come fight for him.

73
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,910
You gonna fight for him now?

74
00:12:23,110 --> 00:12:25,440
To tell you the truth, this isn't so bad.

75
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:29,210
Four walls. A pot to piss in.

76
00:12:30,090 --> 00:12:31,830
I was chained to a wooden post

77
00:12:31,830 --> 00:12:34,140
covered in my own shit for months.

78
00:12:37,210 --> 00:12:39,820
Is that supposed to make me feel better?

79
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,160
Maybe a bit.

80
00:12:44,890 --> 00:12:46,490
I'm sorry, I didn't come sooner.

81
00:12:46,850 --> 00:12:49,120
It's complicated, yes.

82
00:12:50,530 --> 00:12:52,990
-So how is our sister?  -How do you think?

83
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:55,210
Her son died in her arms.

84
00:12:55,870 --> 00:12:57,070
Her son?

85
00:12:58,610 --> 00:12:59,810
Don't.

86
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:06,900
You know what's coming?

87
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:10,100
My trial for regicide. Yes, I know.

88
00:13:11,690 --> 00:13:15,310
I know the whole bloody country thinks I'm guilty.

89
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:17,690
I know that one of my three judges

90
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:20,030
has wished me dead more times than I can count.

91
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:22,290
And that judge is my father.

92
00:13:23,770 --> 00:13:24,920
As for Cersei,

93
00:13:25,230 --> 00:13:26,760
well, she's probably working on a way

94
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:30,000
to avoid a trial altogether by having me killed.

95
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,170
Now that you mention it, she did ask.

96
00:13:33,490 --> 00:13:36,460
So, should I turn around and close my eyes?

97
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,820
Depends.

98
00:13:38,590 --> 00:13:40,120
Did you do it?

99
00:13:40,870 --> 00:13:42,750
The Kingslayer brothers.

100
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:45,440
You like it? I like it.

101
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:50,250
You're really asking if I killed your son?

102
00:13:50,970 --> 00:13:53,400
Are you really asking if I'd kill my brother?

103
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:59,100
How can I help you?

104
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,850
Well, you could set me free.

105
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,270
You know I can't.

106
00:14:05,810 --> 00:14:07,880
Then there's really nothing else to say.

107
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,510
What do you want me to do? Kill the guards?

108
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:12,540
Sneak you out of the city in the back of a cart?

109
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,250
I'm the Lord Commander of the Kingsguard.

110
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:15,840
Sorry, I'd forgotten.

111
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,980
I'd hate for you to do something inappropriate.

112
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:19,220
Inappropriate?

113
00:14:19,220 --> 00:14:22,560
You're accused of killing the king. Freeing you is treason.

114
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:24,470
Except I didn't do it.

115
00:14:24,470 --> 00:14:26,310
Which is why we're having a trial.

116
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:28,570
A trial.

117
00:14:28,850 --> 00:14:31,850
If the killer threw himself before the Iron Throne,

118
00:14:31,850 --> 00:14:33,310
confessed to his crimes,

119
00:14:33,310 --> 00:14:35,780
and gave irrefutable evidence of his guilt,

120
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,440
it wouldn't matter to Cersei.

121
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:40,610
She won't rest until my head's on a spike.

122
00:14:40,610 --> 00:14:42,130
Not just yours.

123
00:14:42,870 --> 00:14:46,070
She's offering a knighthood to whomever finds Sansa Stark.

124
00:14:46,070 --> 00:14:47,670
Sansa couldn't have done this.

125
00:14:47,670 --> 00:14:50,220
She had more reason than anyone in the Seven Kingdoms.

126
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:51,790
Do you think it's a coincidence she disappeared

127
00:14:51,790 --> 00:14:53,320
the same night Joffrey died?

128
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:54,430
No, but.

129
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,740
Sansa's not a killer.

130
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,330
Not yet, anyway.

131
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:17,570
Where are you taking me?

132
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,210
I'm getting married to your Aunt Lysa.

133
00:15:20,430 --> 00:15:22,270
She's waiting for us at the Eyrie.

134
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,660
You'll be safe there.

135
00:15:37,110 --> 00:15:38,770
Did you kill Joffrey?

136
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:41,340
Did I kill Joffrey?

137
00:15:43,370 --> 00:15:45,350
I've been in the Vale for weeks.

138
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,870
I know it was you.

139
00:15:47,350 --> 00:15:50,300
And who helped me with this conspiracy?

140
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,330
Well, there was Ser Dontos.

141
00:15:54,330 --> 00:15:56,480
You used him to get me out of King's Landing,

142
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:59,350
but you would never trust him to kill the king.

143
00:15:59,430 --> 00:16:02,810
-Why not?  -Because you're too smart to trust a drunk.

144
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,600
Then perhaps it was your husband.

145
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:06,460
No.

146
00:16:07,490 --> 00:16:08,790
How do you know?

147
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:11,070
I just do.

148
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:13,700
You're right.

149
00:16:13,830 --> 00:16:15,940
He wasn't involved in Joffrey's death.

150
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:18,040
But you were.

151
00:16:19,310 --> 00:16:22,920
Do you remember that lovely necklace Dontos gave you?

152
00:16:24,010 --> 00:16:27,020
I don't suppose you noticed that a stone was missing

153
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:29,030
after the feast.

154
00:16:30,770 --> 00:16:32,150
The poison.

155
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,870
I don't understand.

156
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:38,360
The Lannisters gave you wealth, power.

157
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,610
Joffrey made you the Lord of Harrenhal.

158
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:43,770
A man with no motive is a man no one suspects.

159
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:46,250
Always keep your foes confused.

160
00:16:46,250 --> 00:16:49,170
If they don't know who you are or what you want,

161
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:52,350
they can't know what you plan to do next.

162
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:56,910
I don't believe you.

163
00:16:58,490 --> 00:17:01,300
If they catch you, they'll put your head on a spike

164
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:02,760
just like my father's.

165
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:06,010
You'd risk that just to confuse them?

166
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:10,960
So many men, they risk so little.

167
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:13,970
They spend their lives avoiding danger.

168
00:17:14,750 --> 00:17:16,250
And then they die.

169
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:21,760
I'd risk everything to get what I want.

170
00:17:23,070 --> 00:17:24,810
And what do you want?

171
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:32,000
Everything.

172
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:37,920
My friendship with the Lannisters was productive.

173
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:39,390
But Joffrey,

174
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:42,680
a vicious boy with a crown on his head,

175
00:17:43,170 --> 00:17:45,050
is not a reliable ally.

176
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:47,160
And who could trust a friend like that?

177
00:17:47,570 --> 00:17:49,270
Who could trust you?

178
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:52,910
I don't want friends like me.

179
00:17:53,090 --> 00:17:55,510
My new friends are predictable.

180
00:17:55,570 --> 00:17:57,420
Very reasonable people.

181
00:17:57,980 --> 00:17:59,500
As for what happened to Joffrey,

182
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:03,690
well, that was something my new friends wanted very badly.

183
00:18:04,570 --> 00:18:06,850
Nothing like a thoughtful gift

184
00:18:06,850 --> 00:18:09,040
to make a new friendship grow strong.

185
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:11,170
I can't believe you're going.

186
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:13,980
Leaving me alone here with these people.

187
00:18:14,190 --> 00:18:16,060
The time has come, my dear.

188
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:18,800
There's nothing more tedious than a trial.

189
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:21,750
Except perhaps these gardens.

190
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,660
If I have to take one more leisurely stroll

191
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:27,890
through these gardens, I'll fling myself from the cliffs.

192
00:18:29,230 --> 00:18:31,290
Have you been to see Tommen yet?

193
00:18:31,410 --> 00:18:32,250
No.

194
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:35,030
Have they even agreed to the match?

195
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,500
No one tells me anything.

196
00:18:37,070 --> 00:18:40,880
I wasn't originally meant to marry your grandfather Luthor, you know.

197
00:18:40,950 --> 00:18:43,550
He was engaged to my sister,

198
00:18:43,730 --> 00:18:45,700
your great-aunt Viola.

199
00:18:46,150 --> 00:18:49,360
I was to be given to some Targaryen or other.

200
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:52,770
Marrying a Targaryen was all the rage back then.

201
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:55,680
But the moment I saw my intended,

202
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:58,650
with his twitchy little ferret's face

203
00:18:58,650 --> 00:19:00,620
and ludicrous silver hair,

204
00:19:00,670 --> 00:19:02,110
I knew he wouldn't do.

205
00:19:02,870 --> 00:19:05,510
So the evening

206
00:19:05,570 --> 00:19:08,420
before Luthor was to propose to my sister,

207
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:11,370
I got lost on my way back from my embroidery lesson

208
00:19:11,370 --> 00:19:14,030
and happened upon his chamber.

209
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:17,430
How absentminded of me.

210
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,530
The following morning, Luthor never made it down the stairs

211
00:19:21,530 --> 00:19:24,620
to propose to my sister 'cause the boy couldn't bloody walk.

212
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:27,620
And once he could, the only thing he wanted

213
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:29,950
was what I'd given him the night before.

214
00:19:30,910 --> 00:19:31,970
I was good.

215
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:34,770
I was very, very good.

216
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:39,360
You are even better.

217
00:19:39,570 --> 00:19:41,240
But you need to act quickly.

218
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:45,040
Cersei may be vicious, but she's not stupid.

219
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:47,850
She'll turn the boy against you as soon as she can.

220
00:19:48,210 --> 00:19:51,010
And by the time you're married, it'll be too late.

221
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:53,190
Luckily for you, the Queen Regent

222
00:19:53,190 --> 00:19:54,880
is rather distracted at the moment.

223
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:57,370
mourning her dear departed boy,

224
00:19:57,850 --> 00:19:59,830
accusing her brother of his murder,

225
00:19:59,830 --> 00:20:01,910
which he didn't commit.

226
00:20:01,970 --> 00:20:03,180
Well, he could have done.

227
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:04,890
He could have done, but he didn't.

228
00:20:04,890 --> 00:20:07,850
-You don't know, Grandmother.  -But I do know.

229
00:20:09,390 --> 00:20:12,120
You don't think I'd let you marry that beast, do you?

230
00:20:13,930 --> 00:20:16,760
What? I don't understand.

231
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:20,270
Don't you worry yourself about all that.

232
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:24,640
You just do what needs to be done.

233
00:20:26,740 --> 00:20:27,720
Bring it through!

234
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:37,550
And again.

235
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:47,310
Very nice. Good.

236
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:50,110
A lot of wildlings fight with a weapon in each hand.

237
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,710
First thing you want to do

238
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:55,800
is disarm them to try and even the odds.

239
00:21:10,050 --> 00:21:11,320
Let's see what you can do.

240
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,210
Olly, you just watch for now.

241
00:21:15,210 --> 00:21:16,420
I can fight.

242
00:21:16,470 --> 00:21:18,230
Have you ever held a sword before?

243
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:20,540
I was the best archer in our hamlet.

244
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:22,670
I was!

245
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:24,480
I believe you.

246
00:21:25,170 --> 00:21:26,940
We'll go hunting for rabbits one day.

247
00:21:27,050 --> 00:21:28,610
Right now, watch and learn.

248
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:31,910
You two.

249
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:35,810
Take it slow, try and disarm each other.

250
00:22:02,150 --> 00:22:03,550
You know how to fight.

251
00:22:04,420 --> 00:22:05,990
You could have gone easier on him.

252
00:22:06,970 --> 00:22:08,610
He wouldn't have learned anything that way.

253
00:22:09,350 --> 00:22:10,700
Lord Snow.

254
00:22:11,950 --> 00:22:13,410
What do you think you're doing?

255
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:16,620
Grenn and I were helping them.

256
00:22:16,620 --> 00:22:18,850
Grenn's a ranger. You're a steward.

257
00:22:18,940 --> 00:22:22,200
Maybe you forgot that while you were off with your wildling bitch,

258
00:22:22,260 --> 00:22:23,280
but I didn't.

259
00:22:24,950 --> 00:22:26,500
Someone has to train them.

260
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:28,120
And that someone isn't you.

261
00:22:28,490 --> 00:22:30,590
Go find a chamber pot to empty.

262
00:22:33,710 --> 00:22:35,340
Go on. Do it.

263
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:37,930
You traitor's bastard.

264
00:22:38,220 --> 00:22:40,010
Give me an excuse.

265
00:22:40,090 --> 00:22:42,430
Mormont's not here to protect you now.

266
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:55,550
Get back to work.

267
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:57,420
Now!

268
00:22:59,250 --> 00:23:01,010
I said, now!

269
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:07,600
The bastard's well-liked. You're not.

270
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:10,160
You think I care if they like me? We're at war.

271
00:23:10,210 --> 00:23:11,030
For now.

272
00:23:11,830 --> 00:23:13,860
But you can't be acting commander forever.

273
00:23:14,450 --> 00:23:15,710
There will be a choosing.

